WEBVTT

01:33.551 --> 01:37.847
DELICIOUS IN DUNGEON

01:44.979 --> 01:46.689
I'm back, Mom.

01:49.526 --> 01:50.735
What's that?

01:50.819 --> 01:52.237
It smells great.

01:53.571 --> 01:55.949
That's because it's your birthday.

01:56.533 --> 01:58.535
It's all your favorite dishes.

01:59.035 --> 02:00.787
Wow, really?

02:00.870 --> 02:02.705
Time to eat up.

02:02.789 --> 02:06.209
See? These are all your favorite...

02:06.793 --> 02:09.212
ingredients from the dungeon.

02:12.632 --> 02:14.467
What's wrong, Marcille?

02:15.969 --> 02:17.137
I had a nightmare.

02:20.140 --> 02:22.308
What's with this smell?

02:22.392 --> 02:24.060
It's the same as in my dream.

02:24.144 --> 02:26.896
Another party is making
breakfast over there.

02:27.397 --> 02:29.190
They're grilling cured pork

02:29.274 --> 02:30.733
and eating it.

02:30.817 --> 02:32.235
I'm so jealous.

02:32.318 --> 02:33.945
How truly terrible.

02:34.028 --> 02:35.947
It's just so tragic.

02:36.030 --> 02:37.031
100 PERSON SURVEY
ON DUNGEON MEALS

02:37.115 --> 02:40.368
When it comes to meals
eaten by young adventurers nowadays,

02:40.451 --> 02:43.288
they have bread, dried meat, and wine.

02:43.371 --> 02:46.457
To build up stamina
for exploring the dungeon,

02:46.541 --> 02:48.293
fat from meats is important.

02:48.376 --> 02:50.044
But that alone is not enough.

02:50.128 --> 02:53.214
Malnutrition is more terrifying
than monsters.

02:54.132 --> 02:55.967
This may sound like a lecture,

02:56.050 --> 03:00.471
but that doesn't mean
our meals are perfect either.

03:00.555 --> 03:05.476
The young elven girl says
she's jealous of their pork,

03:05.560 --> 03:08.396
but that's because her body wants fat.

03:08.479 --> 03:10.231
I just don't want to eat monsters!

03:10.815 --> 03:12.233
And so,

03:12.317 --> 03:15.236
we'll hunt monsters high in fat today.

03:15.320 --> 03:17.822
If we can find eggs, that's even better.

03:17.906 --> 03:19.824
Eggs have all the nutrition you need.

03:19.908 --> 03:22.243
We should proactively harvest them
in the dungeon.

03:23.703 --> 03:25.038
Are you thinking...

03:25.121 --> 03:26.122
Yeah, I am.

03:26.205 --> 03:27.248
What is it?

03:27.999 --> 03:29.292
<i>The body of a chicken.</i>

03:30.043 --> 03:31.169
<i>The tail of a snake.</i>

03:31.920 --> 03:35.131
<i>A creature said to possess deadly venom
in its fangs and claws.</i>

03:35.882 --> 03:37.800
<i>The Basilisk, king of snakes.</i>

03:38.468 --> 03:40.637
Oh, a Basilisk.

03:40.720 --> 03:42.222
Isn't that great, Marcille?

03:42.305 --> 03:43.765
You'll get to eat chicken.

03:45.183 --> 03:48.478
Is that chicken?
Does that really count as chicken?

03:48.561 --> 03:50.563
Isn't it so cool?

03:50.647 --> 03:53.775
I used to think it was cooler
when more species are mixed together.

03:53.858 --> 03:58.363
But with only two types,
they bring out each other's strengths.

03:58.446 --> 04:02.700
I even noticed the beauty of chicken,
something I used to only see as poultry.

04:02.784 --> 04:05.245
It's a simple yet profound combination.

04:05.328 --> 04:08.748
By the way, the Cockatrice
that nests deeper inside

04:08.831 --> 04:11.000
is another kind of snake-tailed animal.

04:11.084 --> 04:14.420
I've always dreamed
of comparing its taste with a Basilisk's.

04:14.504 --> 04:16.381
Why would anyone want that?

04:17.090 --> 04:19.592
That area is a Basilisk nest.

04:21.761 --> 04:23.012
There it is.

04:23.596 --> 04:25.598
Looks like they're freshly laid.

04:26.099 --> 04:28.768
Let's snatch them up
while their mother's gone.

04:28.851 --> 04:30.436
They're so long and narrow.

04:30.520 --> 04:31.354
Hold this.

04:32.146 --> 04:33.731
It's so soft.

04:34.482 --> 04:36.109
A Basilisk cry.

04:36.609 --> 04:37.652
Let's hurry, Senshi.

04:37.735 --> 04:40.238
Wait, we got to wrap this in cloth.

04:43.574 --> 04:44.909
It's the party from earlier.

05:12.854 --> 05:14.731
That's the worst way to run away.

05:14.814 --> 05:16.899
She's basically begging
to get her back kicked.

05:16.983 --> 05:18.318
Go and save her already!

05:26.951 --> 05:29.996
Spread your arms and legs out
to make your body look as big as possible

05:30.079 --> 05:31.748
and make loud sounds to intimidate it.

05:31.831 --> 05:34.751
That'll stop it from coming any further!

05:37.587 --> 05:39.756
I want to pretend that
I'm not associated with him.

05:47.638 --> 05:49.974
<i>Basilisks also have a head on their tail.</i>

05:50.058 --> 05:53.227
<i>It doesn't seem to have a blind spot,
but it only has one body.</i>

05:53.311 --> 05:56.314
<i>If you bait the heads with an attack
from two different directions,</i>

05:56.397 --> 05:57.982
<i>the two brains will confuse the body...</i>

05:59.192 --> 06:00.693
<i>for a single moment.</i>

06:05.490 --> 06:06.574
How are his wounds?

06:07.075 --> 06:08.493
Was he poisoned?

06:08.576 --> 06:09.994
- Y-Yes.
- Laios.

06:10.578 --> 06:12.663
Senshi says he has an antidote.

06:12.747 --> 06:13.998
Really?

06:14.082 --> 06:17.251
I want to use it in today's cooking.

06:17.335 --> 06:19.003
- What?!
- What?!

06:19.087 --> 06:21.255
But this guy's hanging on by a thread!

06:21.339 --> 06:23.674
Instead of taking the antidote alone,

06:23.758 --> 06:25.009
it's tastier when cooked.

06:25.093 --> 06:26.636
Then cook it already!

06:27.512 --> 06:29.806
<i>First, cut off the tail and feet.</i>

06:29.889 --> 06:32.892
<i>Blanch it a bit and pluck its feathers.</i>

06:35.770 --> 06:37.271
It's chicken now.

06:37.355 --> 06:40.691
<i>Take its innards out
and rub your spices on it.</i>

06:40.775 --> 06:44.320
<i>Stuff it with veggies
and finely chopped herbs</i>

06:44.403 --> 06:46.072
<i>and tie up the opening.</i>

06:46.155 --> 06:48.491
<i>Put a skewer through the meat</i>

06:48.574 --> 06:50.576
<i>and roast it thoroughly.</i>

06:51.160 --> 06:52.078
It's done.

06:52.161 --> 06:54.038
Hurry, feed it to him.

06:59.919 --> 07:02.588
The meat's overflowing with juices.
It's delicious.

07:02.672 --> 07:04.090
Sorry about all that.

07:04.674 --> 07:06.300
You all should eat too.

07:06.384 --> 07:07.468
Hold on.

07:07.552 --> 07:09.345
I got to cast a healing spell first...

07:12.431 --> 07:16.269
This is so good!
I could see this at a restaurant in town.

07:16.352 --> 07:18.604
It tastes exactly like chicken.

07:18.688 --> 07:21.232
I heard snake meat
is similar to chicken too.

07:22.692 --> 07:25.820
Sorry, I'll cast my healing spell now.

07:25.903 --> 07:26.737
Oops, wrong item.

07:28.656 --> 07:32.869
I've never had a proper meal
like this before in a dungeon.

07:34.954 --> 07:36.164
Um...

07:36.706 --> 07:41.127
It's been three months
since we started challenging this dungeon,

07:41.711 --> 07:44.630
but we keep getting wiped out
at the same place.

07:44.714 --> 07:50.136
How do we become strong enough
to cook monsters like you all?

07:50.720 --> 07:52.054
Well, that's...

07:52.138 --> 07:54.265
First, improve your diet.

07:54.348 --> 07:56.267
Rethink your circadian rhythm.

07:56.350 --> 07:58.269
And engage in proper exercise.

07:58.352 --> 08:00.897
If you pay attention to
these three things,

08:00.980 --> 08:03.649
your body will naturally get stronger.

08:04.859 --> 08:07.862
<i>What incredible people.</i>

08:08.362 --> 08:10.114
Let's do our best too.

08:15.369 --> 08:18.122
Reaching the third floor today
might be impossible.

08:18.206 --> 08:20.708
It's because we took
our sweet time on that roast.

08:21.292 --> 08:24.378
Apparently, the Red Dragon wakes up
once a month to go hunting.

08:25.087 --> 08:27.798
That was probably
when we ran into it the other day.

08:27.882 --> 08:30.968
Then he's sleeping on a full stomach now.

08:31.052 --> 08:34.305
I'd like to find him
before he gets an empty stomach.

08:34.388 --> 08:36.224
That's why, Marcille,

08:36.307 --> 08:38.434
it'd be great
if we could move things along.

08:43.356 --> 08:44.690
Won't be easy at this rate.

08:45.483 --> 08:47.235
I'm totally fine.

08:47.318 --> 08:49.237
I can easily walk more.

08:49.320 --> 08:50.321
Don't push yourself.

08:50.404 --> 08:51.572
Let's rest a bit.

08:51.656 --> 08:52.907
I'm not pushing myself!

08:52.990 --> 08:54.033
Hey, listen.

08:54.116 --> 08:56.410
If you try to act tough now,

08:56.494 --> 09:00.164
you'll just hurt yourself
and become a burden, got it?

09:00.248 --> 09:01.916
SHOCK

09:01.999 --> 09:04.835
It might be easier
to use a different path.

09:04.919 --> 09:07.088
But the Big Bat outside
will be in our way.

09:07.755 --> 09:10.007
I can use magic on the Big Bats.

09:10.091 --> 09:11.259
No, that's okay.

09:11.759 --> 09:13.594
What about a secret passageway?

09:13.678 --> 09:15.680
More traps, but fewer monsters.

09:15.763 --> 09:17.431
I have trap-disarming spells...

09:17.515 --> 09:20.101
It's faster if Chilchuck disarms them.

09:21.394 --> 09:24.313
We're taking a path
with fewer monsters, huh?

09:24.397 --> 09:26.983
We should secure some foodstuffs then.

09:27.066 --> 09:29.402
Can't we get by on today's leftovers?

09:29.485 --> 09:30.903
We only have meat and eggs.

09:30.987 --> 09:32.738
We need vegetables.

09:32.822 --> 09:35.324
There's a Mandrake colony near here.

09:36.242 --> 09:39.245
Me! I know how to harvest Mandrakes!

09:39.328 --> 09:40.496
Leave it to me!

09:41.747 --> 09:44.667
Mandrakes are fundamental
in magic and medicine.

09:45.293 --> 09:47.128
In other words, my area of expertise.

09:47.211 --> 09:49.672
Everyone, listen to me this time.

09:49.755 --> 09:52.675
Mandrakes scream
when you pull them from the dirt.

09:52.758 --> 09:55.678
It'll make you go insane
or even cause death.

09:56.262 --> 09:58.347
We would get wiped out

09:58.431 --> 10:01.601
and be one step further from saving Falin.

10:01.684 --> 10:03.436
To prevent that...

10:04.145 --> 10:07.273
First, we need a string
and a well-trained dog.

10:07.356 --> 10:08.190
A dog?

10:08.274 --> 10:12.945
We'll tie the Mandrake to the dog's collar
and call the dog over from a distance.

10:13.029 --> 10:15.781
Then, the Mandrake
will be pulled out by the dog.

10:16.282 --> 10:17.867
What'll happen to the dog?

10:18.868 --> 10:19.869
It'll die.

10:19.952 --> 10:21.120
That's awful.

10:21.203 --> 10:22.163
But also,

10:22.246 --> 10:24.123
where are we going to get a dog?

10:24.624 --> 10:27.793
And that method
doesn't seem very efficient.

10:27.877 --> 10:29.712
But at school, we...

10:29.795 --> 10:31.881
Can't we use a long string?

10:31.964 --> 10:32.798
Huh?

10:32.882 --> 10:35.635
Use a string so long
that we won't hear it scream.

10:35.718 --> 10:37.470
Then we won't need a dog.

10:38.054 --> 10:38.971
What?

10:39.055 --> 10:41.140
I'm pretty sure we can't.

10:41.223 --> 10:43.851
Maybe because it's hard to pull?

10:51.734 --> 10:52.943
That scared me.

10:53.027 --> 10:54.695
Was that Marcille?

10:55.655 --> 10:58.908
It won't scream
if you cut its head off beforehand.

10:58.991 --> 11:00.242
That's true.

11:00.326 --> 11:02.078
No, that's too dangerous.

11:02.161 --> 11:04.330
That's how I've eaten them for many years.

11:04.413 --> 11:07.416
That kind of novice mentality
brings the most danger.

11:07.500 --> 11:10.252
But Senshi actually has experience.

11:10.336 --> 11:14.173
Have you ever tried
the method according to the book?

11:14.965 --> 11:17.676
<i>No. I feel so bad for the dog.</i>

11:17.760 --> 11:21.180
Either way, we don't have a dog
nor the time for this.

11:21.263 --> 11:23.682
Sorry, but let's learn how Senshi does it.

11:24.266 --> 11:26.102
<i>If it were that easy,</i>

11:26.185 --> 11:28.687
<i>you'd think it'd be written
in the handbook.</i>

11:29.438 --> 11:30.523
<i>But he's right.</i>

11:30.606 --> 11:33.109
<i>It's not convincing
when I'm only reading from a book.</i>

11:33.192 --> 11:35.694
<i>I shouldn't have them do
something I haven't tried myself.</i>

11:37.154 --> 11:38.697
<i>Something I haven't tried?</i>

11:39.323 --> 11:41.200
<i>Then I'll just have to show them.</i>

11:41.283 --> 11:44.203
<i>I'll prove that my method makes sense.</i>

11:44.286 --> 11:46.038
I'm sorry, Marcille!

11:46.122 --> 11:47.206
I forgive you.

11:47.790 --> 11:50.126
<i>But since I can't use a dog...</i>

11:50.626 --> 11:51.460
<i>A monster!</i>

11:52.294 --> 11:54.880
<i>The monsters in this area are Big Bats.</i>

11:54.964 --> 11:56.966
<i>They should be asleep right now.</i>

11:59.301 --> 12:01.303
<i>I wonder if this will work.</i>

12:01.387 --> 12:03.472
<i>It didn't say how hard you have to pull.</i>

12:04.557 --> 12:07.309
<i>Big Bat nests can be found
through their droppings.</i>

12:07.393 --> 12:10.396
<i>Laios's library of knowledge
is actually coming in handy.</i>

12:10.479 --> 12:13.983
<i>And a place
you can't hear the screams from</i>

12:14.567 --> 12:15.693
<i>would be that tower.</i>

12:23.492 --> 12:24.910
Focus on the target...

12:27.037 --> 12:30.666
<i>Aire Faum Orbis!</i>

12:40.926 --> 12:41.760
All right!

12:44.972 --> 12:46.474
What's that?

12:46.557 --> 12:47.641
Marcille?

12:55.191 --> 12:56.358
Wait.

12:56.859 --> 12:57.902
Wait...

12:58.736 --> 13:00.654
<i>It really is important
to try things first.</i>

13:01.238 --> 13:02.323
<i>If anything,</i>

13:02.406 --> 13:06.035
<i>now I know why Big Bats
shouldn't be used to replace dogs.</i>

13:07.036 --> 13:09.038
Marcille!

13:10.164 --> 13:11.081
Did she die?

13:14.376 --> 13:15.211
She's alive.

13:17.296 --> 13:20.132
Using a Big Bat instead of a dog?

13:20.216 --> 13:21.300
What an idiot.

13:23.385 --> 13:25.721
Hey, Marcille. Can you hear me?

13:26.388 --> 13:28.724
Yes, I am very well.

13:28.807 --> 13:29.975
No, you're not.

13:30.059 --> 13:31.644
She heard the scream.

13:31.727 --> 13:33.062
Let's keep talking with her.

13:33.145 --> 13:35.064
She'll slowly snap out of it.

13:36.482 --> 13:37.566
Why did you do this?

13:37.650 --> 13:40.027
I panicked when I was told
I'd be a burden,

13:40.110 --> 13:40.945
No wait...

13:41.028 --> 13:44.740
...so I wanted to stick it to you guys
and make you bow down to me.

13:44.823 --> 13:45.991
What the heck?

13:46.075 --> 13:47.076
Chilchuck.

13:47.660 --> 13:51.956
I felt alone since I couldn't be
of help to everyone.

13:55.042 --> 13:57.878
The monsters get stronger
as we go deeper into the dungeon.

13:57.962 --> 14:00.631
The thing I can depend on most
is your magic,

14:00.714 --> 14:04.301
so I didn't want to use it up
on such an early floor.

14:05.135 --> 14:07.846
And everyone has strengths and weaknesses.

14:08.430 --> 14:10.558
I want to rely on your strengths.

14:10.641 --> 14:13.477
Someone else will cover
for your weaknesses.

14:14.895 --> 14:16.730
You can depend on us more.

14:19.316 --> 14:20.985
Tell her, Chilchuck.

14:22.152 --> 14:26.740
I really think having you here with us
is a huge help.

14:31.579 --> 14:33.247
Put more feeling into it.

14:33.330 --> 14:36.000
When did you get back to normal?!

14:36.584 --> 14:40.254
I didn't expect a Big Bat too.
What a surprising catch.

14:40.337 --> 14:42.506
How about we make some omelets today?

14:43.507 --> 14:46.343
Is this really a Basilisk egg?

14:46.427 --> 14:48.762
It's completely different
from chicken eggs.

14:48.846 --> 14:50.598
That's how snake eggs are.

14:50.681 --> 14:52.683
Only its tail was a snake.

14:52.766 --> 14:54.643
Its head and body were a chicken.

14:54.727 --> 14:56.812
No, the tail was a chicken.

14:56.896 --> 14:58.147
BODY, TAIL

14:58.898 --> 15:01.901
The color on this one
is different from the rest.

15:01.984 --> 15:03.277
You're right.

15:03.360 --> 15:06.280
Marcille got that one
since it still has a head.

15:09.241 --> 15:12.745
<i>Chop up the Mandrake and sauté it well.</i>

15:12.828 --> 15:15.247
<i>Cover it with the egg.</i>

15:15.331 --> 15:17.541
<i>Once it fluffs up...</i>

15:17.625 --> 15:18.876
It's done.

15:18.959 --> 15:21.545
MANDRAKE AND BASILISK OMELET

15:21.629 --> 15:24.214
The yellow is
way darker than a chicken egg.

15:24.298 --> 15:26.884
This is the Mandrake we harvested.

15:26.967 --> 15:30.554
This one uses the Mandrake
harvested by the elven girl.

15:30.638 --> 15:33.140
You shouldn't rub salt in someone's wound.

15:33.223 --> 15:34.058
Now, now.

15:37.144 --> 15:40.731
Marcille's isn't bitter,
and it has a mild taste.

15:40.814 --> 15:42.399
Yeah, it's delicious.

15:42.483 --> 15:46.070
The screaming must have gotten
the bitterness out.

15:46.654 --> 15:49.907
It's basic cooking knowledge
that going the extra mile improves a dish.

15:49.990 --> 15:52.910
It seems I only sought efficiency

15:52.993 --> 15:55.162
and lost sight of what truly matters.

15:55.245 --> 15:56.914
Thank you, Marcille.

15:57.414 --> 15:59.833
Your knowledge and book are superb.

15:59.917 --> 16:01.752
This isn't a cookbook, you know.

16:02.336 --> 16:04.838
Take this small gift as my thanks.

16:04.922 --> 16:07.424
You can have the most delicious part.

16:10.469 --> 16:12.346
I don't want it!

16:13.097 --> 16:16.684
I'm sick and tired of eating monsters!

16:18.852 --> 16:22.272
Is the shortcut entrance around here?

16:22.356 --> 16:23.273
The entrance?

16:23.357 --> 16:25.192
Laios, give me your sword.

16:32.282 --> 16:33.283
It's here.

16:37.705 --> 16:39.832
What just happened?

16:39.915 --> 16:43.377
Chilchuck is an expert
in detecting traps and picking locks.

16:43.961 --> 16:46.755
Just so you know,
there will be traps everywhere,

16:46.839 --> 16:48.924
so don't do anything unless I tell you to.

16:51.885 --> 16:54.054
What I hate the most

16:54.138 --> 16:56.557
are those who get in the way of my work.

17:05.983 --> 17:07.026
Hold it.

17:22.791 --> 17:24.793
These tiles are safe to step on.

17:33.719 --> 17:35.179
What the heck was that?

17:35.262 --> 17:37.890
I told you to only step
where I told you to.

17:37.973 --> 17:40.642
Your foot's sticking out by so much.

17:40.726 --> 17:42.519
I don't like complicated stuff.

17:42.603 --> 17:44.104
Who cares what you like?

17:44.188 --> 17:46.398
You've got to be more careful.

17:46.482 --> 17:50.194
Some traps are connected
and affect other traps.

17:50.277 --> 17:53.405
If one thing shifts,
all my calculations go out the window.

17:53.489 --> 17:56.658
Just move wherever I tell you to.

18:07.211 --> 18:08.545
Such firepower.

18:08.629 --> 18:09.463
I see.

18:09.546 --> 18:11.465
Traps come in many shapes and forms.

18:11.548 --> 18:13.008
Move your foot already.

18:13.092 --> 18:16.261
Fire traps usually come
as a set with gas or oil.

18:16.345 --> 18:17.179
Oil.

18:17.262 --> 18:19.306
We don't need a dwarf roast.

18:20.057 --> 18:20.933
A roast.

18:21.683 --> 18:22.851
No, wait.

18:23.560 --> 18:24.853
Deep-fried food.

18:24.937 --> 18:25.938
Fried.

18:26.563 --> 18:28.273
<i>Kakiage</i>!

18:29.316 --> 18:31.652
We'll have tempura for lunch today.

18:32.236 --> 18:34.613
Where's the oil trap?

18:34.696 --> 18:36.490
It's not meant for cooking.

18:36.573 --> 18:38.283
Half-foot child.

18:38.367 --> 18:40.619
You are no expert on oil.

18:40.702 --> 18:42.496
I'm not a child.

18:42.579 --> 18:45.791
Vegetable oil is simple
and the highest in supply.

18:45.874 --> 18:47.459
Anyhow, show me the oil.

18:47.543 --> 18:49.962
I'll give up
if it isn't meant for cooking.

18:52.381 --> 18:53.507
Fine.

18:53.590 --> 18:54.883
In exchange,

18:54.967 --> 18:58.387
promise you'll follow
my orders around the traps.

18:58.470 --> 19:02.141
I won't help you
if you don't accept this condition.

19:03.267 --> 19:04.184
I swear it.

19:04.268 --> 19:05.936
I'll help too, if needed.

19:06.019 --> 19:07.146
I won't need it.

19:07.229 --> 19:08.272
Listen.

19:08.355 --> 19:10.274
We each have our own job.

19:10.357 --> 19:13.277
Yours is cooking.
Mine is detecting traps and picking locks.

19:13.360 --> 19:15.154
Marcille's is magic.

19:15.237 --> 19:18.240
I don't say anything
about your cooking methods.

19:18.323 --> 19:21.743
So, please stop interfering with my work.

19:25.789 --> 19:26.874
The treasure vault.

19:26.957 --> 19:30.794
The excessive number of traps here
must be to keep out intruders.

19:33.130 --> 19:34.923
They're secured onto the ground.

19:35.841 --> 19:37.593
I guess I'll try opening one.

19:39.761 --> 19:40.804
Go over there.

19:42.181 --> 19:44.683
He's usually the most mature one.

19:45.267 --> 19:47.686
Having his companions' lives in his hands

19:48.353 --> 19:50.439
is probably putting him on edge.

19:52.649 --> 19:53.609
It's open.

19:54.151 --> 19:57.112
I see. How do we get the oil out?

19:57.196 --> 19:58.572
I don't know.

19:59.156 --> 20:01.116
This is the spout.

20:01.200 --> 20:05.370
Pulling this trigger will release the oil,
but I don't know how much.

20:05.454 --> 20:07.581
I'll have my pot ready then.

20:07.664 --> 20:09.249
Pull the trigger.

20:09.958 --> 20:11.168
No way.

20:11.251 --> 20:12.753
It's probably boiling oil.

20:12.836 --> 20:14.129
Don't be afraid.

20:14.213 --> 20:15.255
I <i>am</i> afraid.

20:18.383 --> 20:20.135
Don't come crying to me later!

20:22.930 --> 20:24.932
So hot!

20:25.641 --> 20:27.226
I told you so.

20:27.809 --> 20:29.436
Are you okay, Senshi?

20:29.519 --> 20:30.812
Your finger's in it!

20:30.896 --> 20:34.691
It's 180 degrees. Perfect for frying food.

20:35.275 --> 20:37.653
You're the type that's okay with heat?

20:37.736 --> 20:41.573
The smell and taste
tell me that it's olive oil.

20:41.657 --> 20:42.574
For real?

20:42.658 --> 20:45.827
They do say this area
originally produced olives.

20:45.911 --> 20:48.330
It's not surprising
that it's used in traps.

20:50.207 --> 20:51.208
You think so?

20:51.291 --> 20:53.543
Either way, I can fry food with this.

20:53.627 --> 20:54.461
Oh, right!

20:54.544 --> 20:57.923
Can we use the blade
from the trap earlier to cut the meat?

20:58.006 --> 21:01.093
No, we don't know
if it'll fall in the exact same place.

21:02.427 --> 21:04.388
I'll leave it to you.

21:04.471 --> 21:07.391
After all, I don't know
how to handle the traps.

21:07.474 --> 21:09.226
Why should I?

21:09.810 --> 21:13.522
Cooking is my job,
so you should follow my directions.

21:13.605 --> 21:16.233
I believe that was our deal.

21:17.276 --> 21:18.735
I never said that.

21:27.369 --> 21:29.413
<i>What am I doing?</i>

21:31.039 --> 21:32.833
I cut the Big Bat.

21:32.916 --> 21:33.750
Okay.

21:35.085 --> 21:38.380
Next, go heat up this oil
at the fire trap from earlier.

21:39.298 --> 21:40.966
What's wrong? Hurry along.

21:44.594 --> 21:48.724
<i>Cut off the Big Bat's thick outer layer
and chop the meat into chunks.</i>

21:48.807 --> 21:50.392
<i>Lightly score the meat,</i>

21:50.475 --> 21:52.894
<i>massage the seasoning in, and let it rest.</i>

21:52.978 --> 21:56.273
<i>Meanwhile, let's prepare
the Mandrake</i> kakiage.

21:56.857 --> 21:59.526
<i>When you peel the Mandrake skin,</i>

21:59.609 --> 22:01.445
<i>it's best to pull the limbs off first.</i>

22:01.528 --> 22:03.697
<i>You can tear them off by hand
if you unravel them.</i>

22:03.780 --> 22:05.532
<i>Completely peel the body</i>

22:05.615 --> 22:08.869
<i>and lightly scrape
the darker parts off the limbs.</i>

22:08.952 --> 22:10.787
<i>Then, we prepare the batter.</i>

22:10.871 --> 22:13.749
<i>Mix a Basilisk egg into the water</i>

22:13.832 --> 22:15.709
<i>and sift flour into the mixture.</i>

22:15.792 --> 22:17.627
<i>Avoid clumps while mixing it</i>

22:17.711 --> 22:19.671
<i>and put the Mandrake in.</i>

22:20.255 --> 22:21.965
How's the fire going?

22:22.049 --> 22:23.300
How would I know?

22:23.383 --> 22:26.386
I've never had to adjust
a trap's firepower before, darn it.

22:28.472 --> 22:30.223
Looks just right.

22:35.270 --> 22:38.148
When it looks like
it won't fall apart, flip it.

22:38.231 --> 22:39.149
Got it?

22:39.232 --> 22:40.317
Okay.

22:44.613 --> 22:45.906
Is it ready?

22:46.573 --> 22:48.950
Dang it. It was too soon.

22:49.534 --> 22:50.911
Maybe the fire's too weak.

22:54.748 --> 22:55.749
It burned.

22:55.832 --> 22:57.250
How's it looking?

22:57.334 --> 22:59.294
It's going horribly.
Can you take it from here?

22:59.377 --> 23:00.921
The fire trap is your job.

23:01.004 --> 23:04.549
I can adjust the fire,
but isn't frying part of your job?

23:04.633 --> 23:06.718
It turns gooey if the fire is weak,

23:06.802 --> 23:09.012
but it burns if it's too strong.

23:09.596 --> 23:12.224
That must mean
it's not a trap-related issue, huh?

23:12.307 --> 23:14.267
Looks almost ready.

23:16.353 --> 23:17.813
The color turned out nicely.

23:18.939 --> 23:20.273
It's done.

23:20.357 --> 23:22.275
MANDRAKE AND BIG BAT KAKIAGE

23:22.359 --> 23:26.154
I never imagined I could eat
fried food in a dungeon like this.

23:27.739 --> 23:29.407
It's fried really well.

23:29.491 --> 23:31.076
We had a good firepower.

23:31.159 --> 23:34.079
You must aim to fry food quickly
with the right temperature.

23:34.162 --> 23:35.622
It gets nice and crispy.

23:35.705 --> 23:39.000
That's pretty hard to do
with an open fire.

23:39.084 --> 23:41.628
I don't think people would do this
on an open fire.

23:41.711 --> 23:45.841
I pass by here often, but who knew
such a convenient room was here?

23:47.717 --> 23:48.844
Listen up.

23:48.927 --> 23:51.346
Don't try this without me here.

23:51.429 --> 23:52.848
You'll die for sure.

23:52.931 --> 23:54.099
I know.

23:54.182 --> 23:57.519
I can never imitate
your trap manipulation skills.

23:57.602 --> 23:59.146
It's truly amazing.

23:59.229 --> 24:02.190
When we go our separate ways someday,

24:02.274 --> 24:05.944
it's unfortunate that I won't be able
to use that trap alone.

24:08.572 --> 24:10.365
I guess I have no choice.

24:10.448 --> 24:12.492
When we have some spare time,

24:12.576 --> 24:14.369
I'll teach you a bit about traps.

24:14.452 --> 24:15.537
Are you sure?

24:15.620 --> 24:18.039
I'm kind of reluctant to do so.

24:19.082 --> 24:23.336
But you know,
you taught me how to cook, Senshi.

24:24.880 --> 24:27.132
<i>Bread cannot replace meat.</i>

24:27.215 --> 24:29.467
<i>Nor can meat replace bread.</i>

24:29.551 --> 24:32.429
<i>But together, they taste even better.</i>

24:34.973 --> 24:38.310
<i>Both food and people remain the same.</i>

24:38.393 --> 24:39.895
<i>Dungeon food.</i>

26:07.816 --> 26:11.861
Subtitle translation by: Chul Kim
